# Mastra v1 patterns (distilled from AGENTS.md)

This repo uses **Mastra v1** (`@mastra/core@^1.x`). Mirror patterns in `src/domains/storyteller/ai/*` and `src/shared/agent-kernel/mastra/*`.

## Imports — use sub-paths, never the package root

- `@mastra/core/agent`, `@mastra/core/tools`, `@mastra/core/mastra`, `@mastra/core/workspace`
- `RequestContext`, **not** `RuntimeContext`

## Tools — two-arg execute

```ts
export const myTool = createTool({
  id: 'my_tool',                       // snake_case, stable
  description: 'When the model should call this — be specific.',
  inputSchema: z.object({ … }),
  outputSchema: z.object({ … }),
  execute: async (inputData, context) => { … },   // separate params, not one object
})
```

Delegate business logic to `src/services/*` when it exists.

## Agents

- No `format` on agents — use `structuredOutput`.
- Model strings: `'openai/gpt-5.6-luna'`, `'anthropic/claude-…'` (`provider/model`). Fast tier = Luna / Gemini Flash via OpenRouter (`TEXT_GEN_FAST_MODEL`).
- Register through the central Mastra instance so storage, workspace, and tracing are shared.
- Wrap runs in `withSpan` where the domain already does.
- Bound memory (`lastMessages: 10` or similar).
- Subagents → `agents` config (`agent-<key>` tools). Mastra workflows ≠ Fabro workflows.

## Don't

- Second Postgres store or Mastra instance.
- `RuntimeContext`, root `@mastra/core` imports, old single-arg `execute`.
- Hardcoded secrets or model strings.
- Remove tracing or shrink memory windows without reason.

## Verify

`npm run typecheck` · `npm run lint` · `npm run test:unit`
